<title>CANADA: Workers strike at Bema's Refugio.</title>
<headline>Workers strike at Bema's Refugio.</headline>
<dateline>VANCOUVER 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bema Gold Corp said late Tuesday that a union representing a minority of workers at its Refugio Mine in Chile has gone on strike.</p>
<p>The mine continues in full operation, Bema said in a statement.</p>
<p>The workers are asking for increased wages and benefits, the company said.</p>
<p>The striking workers represent 26 percent of the total workforce at the mine, which is operated by Compania Minera Maricunga, which is half owned by Bema and half owned by Amax Gold Inc.</p>
<p>The operating company believes its offer made to the union prior to the strike is fair. Management is waiting for a response from the union and believes the dispute can be resolved soon, Bema said.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau 416 941-8100))</p>
</text>
